        "description": "<div id=\"remove_no_follow\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid grid--cols-10@md grid--cols-8@lg article-column\">\n\t\t\t\t\t  <div class=\"col-12 col-10@md col-6@lg col-start-3@lg\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"article-column__content\">\n<section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>The AI industry is moving incredibly fast. It\u2019s almost as though you can close your eyes for ten minutes and wake to find that yet another business-friendly AI tool or service has appeared.\u00a0</p>\n\n\n\n<p>While refreshing, this glut of investment and innovation represents an industry in flux, meaning the most sensible purchasing decisions aren\u2019t yet terribly clear. Which services\u00a0<a href=\"https://www.computerworld.com/article/4074648/apples-big-bang-ai-moment-is-approaching.html\">will stand the test of time</a>? Which will still even be around once investors\u00a0<a href=\"https://www.computerworld.com/article/4050041/how-to-prepare-for-an-ai-bubble-burst.html\">call in their debt</a>? It\u2019s hard to say.</p",
